#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:316
msgid "Conversation History"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: minimum number of messages, 2: maximum number of messages.
#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:319
#, php-format
msgid "Number of earlier chat messages sent to the AI so follow-up questions keep their context. A visitor question and an assistant answer each count as one message, so 4 covers the last two exchanges. Allowed range: %1$d to %2$d. Each message can add up to about 650 input tokens to a follow-up question because it is sent to both the search and the answer requests, so higher values cost more."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:323
msgid "Shortcode and Block Output"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:327
msgid "Search the text that shortcodes and plugin dynamic blocks output"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of posts checked, 2: number of posts expanded per search, 3: cache lifetime in hours.
#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:329
#, php-format
msgid "The standard WordPress search only sees the shortcode tag or block markup itself, so text that a shortcode or a plugin block outputs cannot be found. When enabled, the newest %1$d published posts that contain shortcodes or plugin dynamic blocks are expanded and searched. To keep searches fast, at most %2$d posts are expanded per search and the expanded text is cached for up to %3$d hours or until the post is updated. Turn this off if your site uses many heavy shortcodes or blocks and chatbot replies become slow."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:333
msgid "AI Reply Limit (10 minutes)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:336
msgid "Limit the number of AI replies allowed from the same connection within 10 minutes. Normal short conversations should still pass, while repeated trial-and-error questions are switched to site-search-based guidance only. A practical starting point is around 6 to 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:340
msgid "AI Reply Limit (1 hour)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:343
msgid "Cap the total AI replies allowed from the same connection within 1 hour. Use this to suppress prolonged back-and-forth play while keeping normal customer use available. Set this higher than the 10-minute limit; a practical starting point is around 20 to 40."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:347
msgid "AI Reply Limit (site-wide, daily)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:350
msgid "Hard ceiling on the total number of AI provider calls made across the whole site each day, regardless of visitor IP. This is the main protection against runaway API costs from distributed or automated abuse. Set 0 to disable the cap (not recommended for public sites)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:354
msgid "Trust Proxy Headers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:358
msgid "This site sits behind a trusted reverse proxy or CDN (e.g. Cloudflare, nginx, a load balancer)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-ai-site-search-chatbot-admin.php:360
msgid "When enabled, the visitor IP used for rate limiting is read from forwarded headers (CF-Connecting-IP, X-Real-IP, X-Forwarded-For). Only enable this if a trusted proxy sets those headers; otherwise visitors could spoof them to bypass rate limits. Leave disabled if visitors connect directly to WordPress."
msgstr ""

